{"recall":{"defs":[["Clustering","Grouping unlabelled objects by similarity."],["K-means","Hard clustering minimising within-cluster squared distances."],["K-medoids","K-means variant with actual objects as centres."],["GMM","Weighted sum of Gaussian components."],["Responsibility","Posterior probability that a component generated a point."],["EM","Alternating expectation and maximisation for latent-variable MLE."]],"formulas":["J=\\sum_{n}\\sum_{k}r_{nk}\\|x_n-\\mu_k\\|^2","\\mu_k=\\frac{\\sum_nr_{nk}x_n}{\\sum_nr_{nk}}","p(x)=\\sum_k\\pi_k\\mathcal N(x|\\mu_k,\\Sigma_k)","\\gamma(z_{nk})=\\frac{\\pi_k\\mathcal N(x_n|\\mu_k,\\Sigma_k)}{\\sum_j\\pi_j\\mathcal N(x_n|\\mu_j,\\Sigma_j)}","\\mu_k=\\frac1{N_k}\\sum_n\\gamma(z_{nk})x_n,\\ \\pi_k=\\frac{N_k}N"],"takeaways":["K-means: assign to nearest centre, move centres to means, repeat.","Use restarts and the elbow; scale features.","K-means fails on unequal sizes/densities, odd shapes, outliers; K-medoids for outliers.","GMMs give soft memberships and elliptical clusters.","EM: responsibilities → weighted MLE of π, μ, Σ; watch for collapsing components."],"confused":[["E-step in K-means vs GMM","Nearest centre vs responsibilities."],["SD vs variance in the EM example","The M-step yields variances."],["Hard vs soft","0/1 vs probabilities."],["SSE vs log-likelihood","K-means vs GMM objective."]],"minute":"Unsupervised learning groups unlabelled data. K-means minimises the within-cluster sum of squared distances by alternating an E-step (assign each point to its nearest centre) and an M-step (move each centre to its cluster mean); it converges to a local minimum, so use restarts and choose K with the elbow of SSE. It struggles with clusters of different sizes, densities, non-globular shapes and outliers; K-medoids is more robust to outliers, and distance ratios flag outliers. Gaussian mixture models give soft memberships: p(x) = Σ π_k N(μ_k, Σ_k). EM computes responsibilities, then re-estimates weights, means and covariances, until the log-likelihood stabilises."},"flashcards":[["K-means objective","$J=\\sum_n\\sum_kr_{nk}\\|x_n-\\mu_k\\|^2$"],["E-step (K-means)","Assign to nearest centre"],["M-step (K-means)","$\\mu_k=\\frac{\\sum r_{nk}x_n}{\\sum r_{nk}}$"],["SSE","Sum of squared distances to cluster centres"],["K-means limits","Sizes, densities, shapes, outliers"],["K-medoids","Most central actual object as centre"],["Elbow method","SSE vs K; pick the bend"],["Outlier score","$\\text{dist}(x,\\mu_k)/L_{\\mu_k}$"],["1-of-K coding","Each row of r has one 1"],["Gaussian pdf","$\\frac1{\\sigma\\sqrt{2\\pi}}e^{-\\frac12(\\frac{x-\\mu}\\sigma)^2}$"],["GMM density","$\\sum_k\\pi_k\\mathcal N(x|\\mu_k,\\Sigma_k)$"],["Responsibility","$\\gamma_{nk}=\\frac{\\pi_k\\mathcal N_k}{\\sum_j\\pi_j\\mathcal N_j}$"],["N_k","$\\sum_n\\gamma(z_{nk})$"],["π update","$N_k/N$"],["covariance_type","full, tied, diag, spherical"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what"],"deep":["u-intro"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["u-kmeans"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2","demo"],"deep":["u-estep"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["u-mstep"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["u-algo"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["u-example"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["u-sse"],"viz":["elbowLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["u-init"],"viz":["kmeansStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["u-limits"],"viz":["kmeansLimits"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["u-medoids"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6"],"deep":["u-k"],"viz":["elbowLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8"],"deep":["u-outlier"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["u-hard"],"viz":["softHard"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["u-1ofk"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple"